! tutorial: first_part
! title: Your first part
! about: A plate with two holes and rounded corners: make a shape, name it, change its size, add features. About 5 minutes.
! order: 1

## Make a block
Every part starts with a shape. On the **Model** tab, click **Block…** (in
the Shapes group) and press OK: the form has sizes filled in already. You can also type the
command into the command line at the bottom and press Enter.

Turn the view by dragging with the middle mouse button, or click a face of
the small cube in the top right corner.
hint: BLOCK, 0, 0, 0, 60, 40, 10
check: COUNT("BODY"), GE, 1 ! a body in the model

## Give it a name
A name lets later steps find the body even when earlier steps change.
Click the block in the 3D view, then in the **Properties** panel (right)
double-click the **name** value and type `plate`.
hint: NAME, LAST, plate
check: EXISTS(plate) ! a body called plate

## Change its size
Click the **BLOCK** step in the **History** panel. The Properties panel now
shows that step's numbers. Make the block **80 × 50 × 10**: change `dx` to
80 and `dy` to 50. You may type units too, such as `80 mm`.

Every later step is run again with the new sizes; nothing has to be redone.
hint: PROPS, plate, 1.dx, 80
hint: PROPS, plate, 1.dy, 50
hint: PROPS, plate, 1.dz, 10
check: BBOX(plate).dx, EQ, 80, 0.01 ! 80 long
check: BBOX(plate).dy, EQ, 50, 0.01 ! 50 wide
check: BBOX(plate).dz, EQ, 10, 0.01 ! 10 thick

## Drill two holes
On the **Features** tab, click **Hole…**. Put the first hole at x 15,
y 25 on the top face (z 10) with a diameter of **8**, and press OK. Make the
second one the same way at x 65.
hint: HOLE, plate, 15, 25, 10, 8
hint: HOLE, plate, 65, 25, 10, 8
check: HOLES(plate, 8), GE, 2 ! two holes of 8 in the plate

## Round the corners
Click one of the four upright corner edges, hold **Ctrl** and click the
other three, then right click on one of them and choose **Fillet…** with a
radius of **5**.

Tip: once one corner is done, **Enter on the empty command line** repeats
the last tool on the next pick.
hint: SEL, S, EDGE, AT, 0, 0, 5
hint: SEL, A, EDGE, AT, 80, 0, 5
hint: SEL, A, EDGE, AT, 80, 50, 5
hint: SEL, A, EDGE, AT, 0, 50, 5
hint: FILLET, 5
hint: SEL, NONE
check: STEPS("FILLET"), GE, 1 ! a FILLET step
check: NFACES(plate, "cylinder"), GE, HOLES(plate) + 4 ! all four corners rounded
check: FAILED(), EQ, 0 ! no failed steps

## Done
That is the whole way of working: shapes and features are steps in the
History, and any number in any step can be changed later. Save the part with
**File > Save** (or `SAVE, plate.m3d`).
